I stand in the mobile shop.
The shopkeeper gives me a new SIM card.
I accept the SIM card.
Now I have an Indian phone number!
I look at the packet.
My new number is there.
I read the number aloud.
"Nine, eight, seven, six, five," I say.
"Four, three, two, one, zero."
This number is long.
So I read it again.
"Nine, eight, seven, six, five."
"Four, three, two, one, zero."
Now I remember the number well.
I place the SIM card into my mobile phone.
The signal arrives.
I give the money to the shopkeeper.
"Thank you," I tell him.
He smiles.
Now my life in Mumbai truly begins.
